# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The bottom panel
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Description One pane, showing the register or the report of the selected tab.
Description An optional panel below it holds everything that is not the
Description register itself -- an import waiting to be accepted, or the
Description results of a find -- each in a tab of its own, so more than one can
Description be open and read at once.
Details The panel is open exactly when it has a tab in it, and closes itself
Details when the last one does: accepting or cancelling an import closes that
Details tab, closing a find's results closes that one, and the panel is gone
Details once nothing is left. Opening a new one -- a second find, an import
Details started from another register -- adds a tab rather than replacing
Details what is already open, and the one just opened becomes active, the
Details same rule a register tab already follows.
Details
Details There used to be a Split view on the menu, two registers side by side
Details for reading two accounts at once, and before that an import was shown
Details the same way -- as a second pane beside the register, rather than in
Details this panel. Both are gone. A window that can be left in a two-register
Details state shows two registers on the next launch with nothing to say why;
Details the panel's tabs say why for themselves, and more than one thing can
Details wait to be judged at once, which a single second pane could not do
Details either. Reading two registers at once is worth having again one day as
Details two windows, not as a mode this one can be left in.

Scenario The bottom panel is closed until something opens it
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given transactions are as previous
