Scenario Recategorising from the report moves the figures with it
Description The same operation as in the register, reached from the report. It
Description is the one place where recategorising is expected to change what
Description is on the page: the transaction leaves one category line and joins
Description another, and both totals move.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path               | Type     | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking    | Checking | false       |
| Expenses:Auto      | Expense  | true        |
| Expenses:Auto:Fuel | Expense  | false       |
| Expenses:Groceries | Expense  | false       |
Given transactions are : Transaction
=FebruaryOnChecking
When the transactions are recategorised : TransactionRecategorise
| Ref | Category           |
| T2  | Expenses:Auto:Fuel |
Then report rows are : ReportRow
| Account            | Level | Amount | IsSubtotal |
| Expenses           | 0     | 130.00 | true       |
| Expenses:Auto      | 1     | 130.00 | true       |
| Expenses:Auto:Fuel | 2     | 130.00 | false      |
# The 60.00 of groceries has become fuel, so Groceries has nothing in it and
# is gone from the page while Auto:Fuel holds the whole 130.00. The expenses
# total has not moved, because no amount did.

Attributes TransactionRecategorise
| Attribute | Type           | Default |
