| Date      | Date      |         |
| Payee     | PayeeName |         |
| Blank     | Boolean   | false   |
| TheSame   | Boolean   | true    |

Scenario The report and the register show the same transaction id
Description Shown in both places while the click-through is being checked: it
Description is how a line on one page is known to be the line on the other.
Description The id is a clock reading to the millisecond, so no table can write
Description it down -- what is checked is that it is there and that the two
Description agree. Expected to come off both pages once the navigation is
Description trusted; see the naming rule in Transactions for what it is.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path               | Type    | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking    | Checking | false       |
| Expenses:Auto      | Expense | true        |
| Expenses:Auto:Fuel | Expense | false       |
| Expenses:Groceries | Expense | false       |
Given transactions are : Transaction
=FebruaryOnChecking
When report run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Category     |
| From     | 2026-02-01   |
| To       | 2026-02-28   |
| Interval | Whole        |
| Detail   | Transactions |
Then the transaction id shown is : IdShown
| Date       | Payee         | Blank | TheSame |
| 2026-02-01 | Shell         | false | true    |
| 2026-02-05 | Harris Teeter | false | true    |
| 2026-02-10 | Shell         | false | true    |
# Three transactions, three ids, and each one the same string in the report as
# in the register. Two transactions sharing an id would make the click-through
# land on the wrong line and is the thing this is really watching for.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The listings, and the menu on the tree
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Description Two windows that show the chart itself rather than the work done in
Description it -- one of the accounts, one of the categories -- and the menu
Description reached by right-clicking a line of the tree on the left.
Details The tree answers "where am I working". It groups the real accounts
Details under headings, totals each heading, leaves the hidden ones out until
Details they are asked for, and shows no categories at all. Every one of those
Details is right for working and wrong for maintaining: a category can only be
Details renamed if it can be found, and a hidden account can only be brought
Details back if it can be seen.
Details
Details So each listing is one line per node, every node, in path order, with no
Details headings and nothing left out. The account listing carries the bank and
Details the number from the account's own dialog, because seeing them together
Details is how a statement is matched to the account it belongs to; the
Details category listing carries the alias, because that is the only place it
Details is ever read.
Details
Details Both are windows of their own and not tabs. A tab is something to come
Details back to, and a listing is opened to find one node, change it, and close
Details again. Which menu they are on is not a table's business; that they are
Details reached from a menu rather than from the tree is, because the tree is
Details the thing they exist to get around.
Details
Details Clicking a line opens the editor of the thing on that line, so finding
Details and changing are one gesture rather than two. The menu on the tree
Details opens the same editor, because there would be no sense in one account
Details having two settings windows depending on where it was clicked.

Attributes AccountListingRow
Description One line of the account listing, in path order so a parent reads
Description above its children.
| Attribute     | Type        | Default  |
| Path          | AccountPath |          |
| Type          | AccountType | Checking |
| Placeholder   | Boolean     | false    |
| Hidden        | Boolean     | false    |
| Bank          | Text        | none     |
| AccountNumber | Text        | none     |
| Balance       | Money       | 0.00     |

Attributes CategoryListingRow
Description One line of the category listing, in path order.
| Attribute   | Type        | Default |
| Path        | AccountPath |         |
| Type        | AccountType | Expense |
| Placeholder | Boolean     | false   |
| Hidden      | Boolean     | false   |
| Alias       | Text        | none    |

Attributes ListingRowSelect
Description The line clicked, named by the path on it.
| Attribute | Type        | Default |
| Path      | AccountPath |         |

Attributes EditorOpened
Description Which editor came up and what it came up on. What the account
Description settings window holds is specified in Accounts; what is said here
Description is only that clicking a line opens it on the right node.
| Attribute | Type | Default |
| Window    | Text |         |
| Target    | Text | none    |

Attributes TreeNode
Description A line of the tree on the left, named the way the tree shows it --
Description a group heading by its heading, an account by its path.
| Attribute | Type | Default |
| Node      | Text |         |

$WIP
Scenario The account listing is every account, one line each
Description A placeholder is a line, a hidden account is a line, there are no
Description group headings, and the categories are not here at all -- they have
Description a listing of their own. Compare the account list scenarios above,
Description where each of those four is the other way round.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path               | Type       | Placeholder | Hidden |
| Assets             | Checking   | true        | false  |
| Assets:Checking    | Checking   | false       | false  |
| Assets:Old Savings | Savings    | false       | true   |
| Liabilities:Visa   | CreditCard | false       | false  |
| Expenses:Groceries | Expense    | false       | false  |
When account listing opened
Then account listing rows are : AccountListingRow CompareOnly
| Path               | Type       | Placeholder | Hidden |
| Assets             | Checking   | true        | false  |
| Assets:Checking    | Checking   | false       | false  |
| Assets:Old Savings | Savings    | false       | true   |
| Liabilities:Visa   | CreditCard | false       | false  |
# Four lines for five rows of chart. Expenses:Groceries is a category and is in
# the other listing.

